  <knowledge>
    - `list systems <subnet>` outputs IP addresses of all systems in the subnet sorted ascending in
  the format '<ip> ... <ip>'.
    - `send packet <ip> <ip>` outputs the IP address of each hop on the route, including sender and
  receiver, in the format '<ip> ... <ip>'.
    - `list range <subnet>` outputs the first and last IP address of the subnet in the format '<ip>
  <ip>'.
    - `list subnets` outputs all subnets sorted ascending by network address in the format '<subnet>
   ... <subnet>'.
    - Networks are defined using the Mermaid syntax.
    - The `load network` command loads a specified file, parses its content, and validates the
  contained network.
    - The `load network` command prints the file content verbatim for testing purposes.
    - If `load network` is executed multiple times and the new network is valid, the new network
  overwrites the old one.
    - Only routers may have connections to routers in other subnets (inter-subnet router-to-router
  connections are restricted to routers).
    - On successful execution `add connection` produces no output (except possibly an error message
  on failure).
    - On successful execution `add computer` produces no output (except possibly an error message on
   failure).
    - On successful execution `remove connection` produces no output (except possibly an error
  message on failure).
    - On successful execution `remove computer` produces no output (except possibly an error message
   on failure).
  </knowledge>
